Banking Data Platform

An event-driven banking data processing platform built with Java 21, Spring Boot, and Clean Architecture principles.
This project demonstrates a production-oriented backend design using streaming, search, and containerization.

🚀 Features

Event-driven architecture with Apache Kafka

Clean Architecture (Domain / Application / Infrastructure / API / Bootstrap)

Transaction processing pipeline

Elasticsearch indexing and search

REST API for querying transactions

Retry & Dead Letter Queue (DLQ) for Kafka consumers

Docker & Docker Compose for one-command local setup

🧱 Architecture Overview
Client
  ↓
REST API (banking-api)
  ↓
Application Use Cases (banking-application)
  ↓
Ports (Interfaces)
  ↓
Infrastructure Adapters
    - Kafka Consumer
    - Elasticsearch Adapter
  ↓
Domain Model (banking-domain)

Key Principles

Business logic is framework-agnostic

Spring is used only for wiring and adapters

Dependencies always point inward

🛠️ Tech Stack

Java 21

Spring Boot 3

Apache Kafka

Elasticsearch

Spring Data Elasticsearch

Docker & Docker Compose

Maven (Multi-module)

📦 Modules
Module	Description
banking-domain	Core domain model and business rules
banking-application	Use cases and ports (application logic)
banking-infrastructure	Kafka & Elasticsearch adapters
banking-api	REST API (Inbound adapter)
banking-bootstrap	Spring Boot entry point & wiring
🐳 Running the Project (Docker)
1️⃣ Build the application image
docker build -t banking-data-platform .

2️⃣ Start all services
docker compose up


This will start:

Kafka

Zookeeper

Elasticsearch

Banking Application

🔍 API Usage
Search Transactions by Customer ID
GET http://localhost:8081/api/transactions?customerId=123


Response Example

[
  {
    "transactionId": "tx-1",
    "customerId": "123",
    "accountId": "acc-99",
    "amount": 1500,
    "currency": "USD",
    "transactionType": "DEPOSIT",
    "channel": "MOBILE",
    "transactionTime": "2025-01-01T10:15:30Z",
    "status": "COMPLETED"
  }
]

📡 Kafka Topics
Topic	Purpose
banking.transaction.events	Main transaction events
banking.transaction.retry	Retry topic
banking.transaction.dlq	Dead Letter Queue
🧪 Testing Strategy

Domain and application layers are unit-tested

Use cases are tested without Spring context

Infrastructure concerns are isolated

🧠 Design Highlights

No Spring annotations in Domain or Application layers

Use cases wired in a dedicated bootstrap (composition root)

Retry & DLQ handled centrally via Spring Kafka error handling

Docker builds optimized using multi-stage builds

